<Base title="About Tidewater | Operator-Led Bid Desk" description="Tidewater Advisory LLC is an independent government bid desk serving DMV operators and nearby markets.">
<section class="section"><div class="container alt-hero"><p class="eyebrow">About Tidewater</p><h1>Where the river meets the tide.</h1><p class="lead">Built around the people doing the work: the restaurant owner, the service manager, the team that has to show up and deliver what was promised.</p></div></section>
<section class="section reverse"><div class="container grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">The name</p><h2>From the tidal rivers to the coast.</h2></div><div><p>The Potomac and Anacostia meet in a working waterfront shaped by the tide. Tidewater speaks to our starting point in DC and our natural reach through Annapolis toward Charleston.</p><p>Local knowledge, practical operations and a willingness to read the fine print.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Founder</p><h2>Built by an operator.</h2><p>James C. Simpson III has spent twenty years in hospitality, including seven helping run a three-location Washington restaurant group with about 100 employees and more than $10 million in annual revenue. He served as beverage director, launched the delivery-first Ghostburger as managing partner at the start of the pandemic, and founded Prepshift, an operations consultancy for restaurant and hospitality operators.</p><p>He has priced the job, staffed the shift and carried the payroll. Tidewater puts that operator’s view behind every bid.</p><p class="fine">Based in Washington, DC.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>How we work</h3><ul><li>Show the source. Especially on award prices and contract requirements.</li><li>Tell the operator when a bid is a bad fit.</li><li>Write for one firm per solicitation.</li><li>Use the client's real experience, not inflated claims.</li><li>Price the work clearly and let the client control final approval.</li></ul></div></div></section>
